# .gitignore - the public OUTPOST tree.
#
# Personal configuration reads from a resolved directory OUTSIDE this tree
# (see docs/config-model.md). So the rule below is default-deny for the shapes
# a config file takes - an .env, a Caddyfile, a conf dir, an appdata dir -
# anywhere in the tree, with one allowlist: the shipped examples under
# config.example/. A config value has nowhere in this tree to live. That is the
# point: the working tree cannot hold personal state by habit, so the failure of
# a `git add -A` publication or a lost disk holding the only copy cannot happen.
#
# gitignore is first-match-wins per path, so an un-ignore only wins when it comes
# after the ignore it answers. The allowlist is therefore last.

# --- Config shapes: denied anywhere in the tree -------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local.*
**/compose.env
**/app.env
**/outpost.env
**/Caddyfile
**/docker-compose.override.yml
**/conf/
**/appdata/
**/APPDATA/
**/user-data/
**/*.custom
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.bak
**/*.bak.*

# --- Non-config shapes: kept from the original ignore list --------------------
# Service data and working directories that are not personal config, and a vendor
# compose file that is replaced on every upgrade.
WIP/
CUSTOM/
db/
mongodb/data/
temp/
immich/docker-compose.yml

# --- Allowlist: the one config that may be committed -------------------------
# Kept so template/.env.example survives **/.env.*.
!**/.env.example
# Dropped was the old !**/Caddyfile.example: the Caddyfile example now ships once,
# under config.example/00_proxy/Caddyfile. The examples are the only config-shaped
# things this tree commits, so this is the only rule that lets a config path in.
!config.example/**
